Vacuum systems — Vincent Baglin and Roberto Kersevan (@gas-vacuum-systems: 0, is #reference, #part-of @gas-sources) { r_1K9ATEHFM7ET2H8TRHC3QNCRFN
Vincent Baglin and Roberto Kersevan. *Vacuum systems*, chapter II.8 in *Proceedings of the Joint Universities Accelerator School: Courses and exercises*, CERN-2024-003, published 19 November 2024, 80 PDF pages. [Official publication](https://e-publishing.cern.ch/index.php/CYRSP/article/view/1624), [complete chapter](https://e-publishing.cern.ch/index.php/CYRSP/article/download/1624/1336/7999), DOI 10.23730/CYRSP-2024-003.1259.

Read the entire chapter and solve its exercises before consulting section II.8.8. Basic quantities and instrumentation lead into outgassing, cryogenic vacuum, interactions with particle beams, pressure profiles and a large operating system. Use the accelerator cases to examine general gas/surface mechanisms, preserving their application-specific assumptions.

Metadata, section structure and selected pump, outgassing and getter passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. The complete file was downloaded outside the repository. Check definitions and units independently: in particular, state which way a compression ratio is formed before comparing equations or values. The entire exercise programme and cited primary literature have not been independently reproduced.

CC BY 4.0; retain authorship and separate component credits. All source documents, figures and external data remain references.

